%% hld/07 - staged rollout with device-side autonomous revert
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Stable

  Stable --> Canary: operator starts rollout
  Canary --> Soak: 1% of fleet updated
  Soak --> Halted: health gate FAILS
  Soak --> Wave5: health gate passes after soak

  Wave5 --> Halted: regression detected
  Wave5 --> Wave25: gate passes
  Wave25 --> Halted: regression detected
  Wave25 --> Full: gate passes
  Full --> Stable: fleet converged

  Halted --> Stable: rolled back, incident opened

  state "Device-side (independent of the controller)" as Dev {
    [*] --> Applying
    Applying --> SelfTest: image written, one-shot boot flag set
    SelfTest --> Confirmed: healthy AND controller reachable
    SelfTest --> Reverting: watchdog fires OR health check fails
    Reverting --> LastKnownGood: bootloader falls back
    LastKnownGood --> [*]: reports the failure upstream
    Confirmed --> [*]: marks slot permanent
  }

  note right of Halted
    A controller-driven rollback is useless when
    the bad config broke connectivity TO the controller.
    That is what the device-side path exists for.
  end note
